      "content": "ok, i hear you on the systemic bias part. that's actually a huge part of my paper. but even if those traits aren't \"inherent,\" isn't it still sociologically relevant to discuss the *perceptions* of these traits? like, if there's a widespread social perception that certain groups are seen as more \"confrontational\" in high-stress settings, even if that's a biased projection, wouldn't that perception itself be a measurable sociological phenomenon? i'm trying to understand the gap between the reality and the perceived behavioral archetypes that people actually encounter in professional environments.",
